//? Title: Stacked RNN: Explicit State, Masks and Updates
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The original stacked_rnn experiment, with reusable native tensor components and a complete editable C++ fitting program. Source seeds, budgets, derivative checks and baseline limitations are retained.
)
\toc


> Read the component and its controls

The upper cell consumes the current lower state at every timestep; separate initial-state and input-Jacobian probes expose both paths.

The source uses512 fitting,128 validation and128 test marked sequences; twelve padded steps, two channels and twelve units. Adam(.01),32-row batches and three epochs give48 updates per policy. Targets are balanced marker signs; the marked token precedes the last valid token.

The actual source graph has506 learned values. The complete program records initialization, first update, every validation epoch, final parameters and source invariance probes.

